.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt NVFATBIN 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvfatbin ,
.Nm fatbinary
.Nd wrap device payloads in the cuda-native fatbinary stub
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 64
.Fl -create
.Ar file
.Fl -image3 Ns = Ns Cm kind= Ns Ar kind Ns Cm ,sm= Ns Ar number Ns Cm ,file= Ns Ar input
.Op Ar image ...
.Pp
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
and its installed alias
.Nm fatbinary
are the same POSIX shell program.
They accept the option subset that clang 23 emits when it collects CUDA device
images.
At least one
.Fl -image3
is required.
Images are retained in argument order; each kind is
.Cm elf
or
.Cm ptx ,
and each SM value is a decimal number.
.Pp
The output starts with the line
.Li CUDA-NATIVE-STUB-FATBIN 1 .
One metadata line per input follows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
member kind=KIND sm=N size=BYTES sha256=HEX
.Ed
A line containing only
.Li ---
separates the metadata from the complete member payloads, which follow in
argument order with no added bytes.
The size and SHA-256 are measured over each unchanged input.
The output is built privately in its destination directory and renamed into
place only after every image has been read.
.Pp
.Fl 64
is accepted for clang compatibility.
.Fl -create
also accepts an equals sign before its value.
.Fl h
and
.Fl -help
print usage.
Every unsupported option, malformed image specification or extra argument is
refused instead of being ignored.
.Pp
.Fl -version
prints
.Ql nvfatbin (cuda-native) VERSION stub .
With
.Fl -json
it prints one JSON object containing
.Dv tool ,
.Dv version ,
.Dv version_major ,
.Dv version_minor ,
.Dv version_patch ,
.Dv stub
and
.Dv track .
The version string and its three integer parts come from
.Dv CUDA_NATIVE_VERSION
in
.Pa sdk/include/cuda.h
when
.Pa mksdk.sh
installs the tool.
The object validates against
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/cuda-native-tool-1.schema.json .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CUDA_NATIVE_TRACE
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_TRACE
When nonempty, append one JSON record after a successful container write.
The record has
.Dv tool ,
.Dv schema ,
.Dv output ,
.Dv images
and
.Dv stub
fields.
The image array records each kind, numeric SM value and input path in order.
The record is validated by
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/nvfatbin-trace-1.schema.json
in the SDK tree.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
In detail, exit status 0 means that the stub container was written, 2 reports
usage or an unsupported argument, and 1 reports an input, output or trace
error.
A failed image read leaves no output at the requested path.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Wrap one ELF-labelled payload and its PTX source:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fatbinary -64 --create kernel.fatbin \e
    --image3=kind=elf,sm=121,file=kernel.o \e
    --image3=kind=ptx,sm=121,file=kernel.ptx
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvptxas 1 ,
.Xr libcudart-stub 3 ,
.Xr cuda-native-toolchain 7
.Sh CAVEATS
The container is a cuda-native diagnostic format, not an NVIDIA fatbinary.
It neither assembles PTX nor makes device code executable.
The stub runtime validates and counts its metadata for host-side registration,
but never registers its contents with a GPU.
No NVIDIA CUDA toolkit file is used.
